#lang rmn/v2
(map
  ("type" "IndependentImprovementBoardForagingLaw")
  ("version" 16)
  ("supplier" "one sovereign supplier settlement")
  ("precondition" "One signed A2A 1.0 Message carries one canonical RMN/CBOR ImprovementMarketSupplierIncitementRequest addressed to this supplier. The supplier has explicit treaties naming standard ActivityPub customer faces and A2A Agent Cards. Supplier resource pressure and self-mutation history belong only to this settlement's append-only witness journal record.")
  ("operation" "Observe this supplier's exclusive execution lane from typed capacity epochs, reservations, consumptions, and settlements. Serialize one foraging pulse before selecting an award or crossing a paid boundary. Read configured customer ActivityPub outboxes; bind a fresh supplier reservation before bidding; consume only the awarded reservation; and settle every consumed reservation only after a known submission, refusal, or pre-border terminal outcome. Before award fulfillment append its deterministic request identity. Before customer submission append the exact authored ActivityStreams object and operation. Lost responses remain recoverable and replay those exact objects; they are never terminalized or regenerated. Hire the software mission provider only through signed A2A and return proposal bytes or typed refusal through the customer's ActivityPub ingress. Fold public capability gaps under supplier-local policy into a capacity opportunity, adjacent capability opportunity, or founder-facing formation lead without changing capacity, capability, or enterprise topology. A standing supplier decision may publish one provider-neutral self-improvement lot. For one recipe-bound capability lot, acquire one OS-enforced settlement lock before reading or claiming its unfinished state and retain that lock through procurement, intention, actuation, schedule transition, and settlement. Append a deterministic acceptance-procurement intent before procurement and an implementation-mission intent before mission execution; ambiguous results replay those request identities without repurchase under another identity. Procure and execute a protected behavioral acceptance capsule, retain every provider identity as provenance without using identity inequality as evidence, canonicalize every allowlisted target path, and stage exact proposal bytes. Before any live byte changes, fsync canonical-CBOR prepared intent bytes to a sibling temporary file, atomically publish the write-once recovery cell without replacement, fsync its directory, and append the same prepared execution intent to witness journal; the recovery cell is reconciled into witness journal and is never an alternate history. A later pulse resumes the same prepared intent instead of purchasing or mutating twice. Live bytes may move only from every prepared before-image toward its matching after-image; unrelated drift is preserved. Before asking ScheduleDelivery to renew, append the exact ActivityStreams ScheduleTransitionRequest as a supplier-local transition intent. ScheduleDelivery atomically records its deterministic successor registration and exact predecessor retirement in one transition; response loss or a later supplier settlement failure replays that exact request to reconcile the existing transition and never authors a second successor. An ambiguous renewal outcome preserves the after-image until that exact transition is observed. Public GitHub test compute resolves one admitted tag to its pinned runner commit, requires an active exact-tag ruleset that denies update and deletion with no bypass actor, and verifies the remote workflow's Git blob and SHA-256 bytes against its local bounded workflow before dispatch. Append settlement only after exact predecessor retirement; terminal failure only before any external intent or after exact rollback.")
  ("postcondition" "Every capacity act, publication, bid, award admission, provider request intent, customer outbound intent, provider refusal, customer decision, foldback, capability-gap disposition, self-investment decision, prepared execution intent, schedule-transition intent, recovery residue, exact schedule transition, settlement, and resource outcome has typed supplier-local witness history. A completed publication is not processed twice. An admitted but unsettled border effect remains recoverable and cannot authorize a second identity, procurement, fulfillment, submission object, workflow revision, successor schedule, or unjournaled mutation. A failed witness journal prepared-intent append preserves the exact canonical bytes in supplier data and retries that append without repurchasing. Unknown provider, customer, or schedule outcomes never authorize terminal closure or destructive rollback. Unknown, stale, or occupied capacity never authors a bid. Only supplier-integrated work or exact customer-accepted foldback may train a deterministic resolver.")
  ("refusal" "Refuse noncanonical or foreign pulses; undeclared ActivityPub or A2A faces; package-import or local-process inter-enterprise paths; changed opportunities or expanded authority; absent capacity; foreign reservations; unsafe or excessive proposal bytes; symlinks and path escapes; actuation-lock contention; unrelated live drift; failed staged or behavioral verification; unjournaled or conflicting schedule-transition requests; unproved schedule retirement or compensation; mutable, moved, or byte-changed public-compute workflows; customer mutation authority; upward inference escalation; and work outside supplier qualifications. Provider identity overlap is provenance and never a refusal gate.")
  ("effects" ("supplier-local-capacity-observation" "supplier-local-capacity-reservation" "supplier-authored-bid" "hired-activitypub-protocol-projection" "hired-software-mission-execution" "supplier-local-capability-gap-foldback" "supplier-self-investment-demand-publication" "protected-oracle-procurement" "supplier-local-proposal-staging" "supplier-local-recoverable-mutation" "atomic-closure-bound-schedule-renewal" "founder-facing-formation-market-lead-delivery"))
  ("invariants" ("canonical-rmn-a2a-control-face" "one-software-mission-executor" "finite-supplier-owned-activitypub-treaties" "no-global-board-registry" "no-global-capacity-pool" "no-mission-queue" "no-local-process-inter-enterprise-fallback" "no-customer-territory-write" "unknown-capacity-is-not-zero-priced-capacity" "no-oversubscription" "proposal-is-not-customer-acceptance" "provider-identity-is-provenance-not-proof" "behavioral-acceptance-discharges-the-obligation" "one-foraging-admission-lock" "border-intent-before-external-effect" "ambiguous-submission-is-recoverable" "one-self-improvement-lock-from-admission-through-settlement" "canonical-paths-before-intention" "prepared-intent-before-live-effect" "crash-atomic-write-once-recovery-cell" "canonical-cbor-recovery-copy-in-data-is-not-authority" "recover-intent-without-reprocurement" "compare-and-write-and-restore-share-one-lock" "transition-request-intent-before-clockkeeper-effect" "reconcile-one-clockkeeper-transition" "atomic-successor-predecessor-transition" "ambiguous-renewal-preserves-successor-runtime" "immutable-ruleset-pinned-byte-verified-public-workflow" "no-upward-model-escalation" "clock-does-not-own-work")))
